2.
Definitions.
- In these rules, unless the context otherwise requires,
(a)
"Act" means the Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises Development Act, 2006 (27 of 2006);
(b)
"Section" means a Section of the Act;
(c)
"Arbitration and Conciliation Act" means the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996 (26 of 1996);
(d)
"Council" means the Micro and Small Enterprises Facilitation Council, established by the Government under Section 20
of the Act;
(e)
"Institute" means any institution or centre providing alternate dispute resolution services referred to in Sub-sections (2)
and (3) of Section 18 of the Act;
(f)
"Chairperson" means the Chairperson of the Council appointed under clause (i) of Sub-section (1) of Section 21 of the
Act;
(g)
"Member" means a member of the Council;
(h)
"Government" means the Government of Orissa;
(i)
The words and expressions used and not defined, but defined in the Act shall have the meanings as respectively
assigned to them in the Act.
